\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Determined the unique scalar-flat radial exterior mass from positive round mean curvature in the time-symmetric ansatz; not general stationary existence/uniqueness.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the supplied definition, catalogue wording, source qualifications and reference entries for 30004802. The historical source/context and inherited status are retained; no fresh literature or novelty certification is claimed. No external theorem is used without proof in this attempt; explicit model assumptions are distinguished from facts about the source model.

\paragraph{A round time-symmetric exterior calculation.} Restrict to \(k=0\) and a spherical exterior metric \(g=dr^2/f(r)+r^2d\Omega^2\), \(f>0\). Computing its scalar curvature yields \(R_g=2(1-f-rf')/r^2\). Thus the time-symmetric vacuum constraint gives \((rf)'=1\), or
\[
 f(r)=1-2m/r.
\]
At a round boundary of radius \(R\), the unit normal is \(\sqrt f\,\partial_r\) and the area derivative gives \(H=2\sqrt{f(R)}/R\). Accordingly the boundary pair \((R,H)\), with \(H>0\), determines
\[
 m=\frac R2\left(1-\frac{H^2R^2}{4}\right).
\]
The radial family is asymptotically flat and has \(f>0\) for \(r\ge R\). The momentum boundary component is zero since \(k=0\). This verifies uniqueness of the mass parameter within this restricted radial ansatz.
\paragraph{Limits of the reduction.} It proves neither uniqueness among nonspherical stationary exteriors nor an extension for arbitrary source boundary tensors. The source allows expansion that is merely not everywhere nonpositive, substantially weaker than the pointwise \(H>0\) used here with \(k=0\). Also regular dominant-energy interiors may constrain the allowed round data; none is constructed for every algebraic pair.
\paragraph{First gap.} The unrestricted stationary boundary-value system needs existence and uniqueness modulo boundary-compatible diffeomorphisms, with all components of the supplied Bartnik data. The elementary radial ODE does not provide those elliptic/gauge estimates. The recovered full boundary formula and its source qualification are retained, with no fresh general-conjecture status claim.

